{
  "mn109:0.1": "Middle Discourses 109 ",
  "mn109:0.2": "The Longer Discourse on the Full-Moon Night ",
  "mn109:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn109:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in the stilt longhouse of Migāra’s mother in the Eastern Monastery. ",
  "mn109:2.1": "Now, at that time it was the sabbath—the full moon on the fifteenth day—and the Buddha was sitting in the open surrounded by the Saṅgha of monks. ",
  "mn109:3.1": "Then one of the monks rose from his seat, arranged his robe over one shoulder, raised his cupped palms toward the Buddha, and said, ",
  "mn109:3.2": "“Sir, I’d like to ask the Buddha about a certain point, if you’d take the time to answer.” ",
  "mn109:3.3": "“Well then, monk, take your own seat and ask what you wish.” ",
  "mn109:3.4": "That monk took his seat and said to the Buddha: ",
  "mn109:4.1": "“Sir, are these the five grasping aggregates: ",
  "mn109:4.2": "form, feeling, perception, choices, and consciousness?” ",
  "mn109:4.3": "“Yes, they are,” replied the Buddha. ",
  "mn109:4.4": "",
  "mn109:4.5": "Saying “Good, sir”, that monk approved and agreed with what the Buddha said. Then he asked another question: ",
  "mn109:5.1": "“But sir, what is the root of these five grasping aggregates?” ",
  "mn109:5.2": "“These five grasping aggregates are rooted in desire.” ",
  "mn109:6.1": "“But sir, is that grasping the exact same thing as the five grasping aggregates? Or is grasping one thing and the five graspi